From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: icc-bwmon: keep applied bandwidth after failed OPP

The OPP/interconnect transaction can fail. Keep current_kbps at the last
successful value so a later IRQ can retry the unchanged target, and report
the error with a rate limit. Preserve threshold rearming and OPP reference
cleanup. This does not qualify hardware demand voting or timer/IRQ retries.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
@@ -648,6 +648,7 @@
 	unsigned int irq_enable = 0;
 	struct dev_pm_opp *opp, *target_opp;
 	unsigned int bw_kbps, up_kbps, down_kbps, meas_kbps;
+	int ret;
 
 	bw_kbps = bwmon->target_kbps;
 	meas_kbps = bwmon->target_kbps;
@@ -689,8 +690,11 @@
 	if (bwmon->target_kbps == bwmon->current_kbps)
 		goto out;
 
-	dev_pm_opp_set_opp(bwmon->dev, target_opp);
-	bwmon->current_kbps = bwmon->target_kbps;
+	ret = dev_pm_opp_set_opp(bwmon->dev, target_opp);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err_ratelimited(bwmon->dev, "Failed to set bandwidth OPP: %d\n", ret);
+	else
+		bwmon->current_kbps = bwmon->target_kbps;
 
 out:
 	dev_pm_opp_put(target_opp);
